Rules:
  [J1] Use `async/await` for asynchronous operations.
  [J2] Always handle promise rejections with `try/catch`.
  [J3] Use `Promise.all` for parallel independent operations.
  [J4] Use `Promise.allSettled` when partial failure is acceptable.
  [J5] Use `AbortController` for cancellable operations.
  [J6] Use event loop phases knowledge for performance.
  [J7] Avoid blocking the event loop with CPU-heavy tasks.
  [J8] Use Web Workers for CPU-intensive work in browser.

Pros:
  - Simple async syntax
  - Good ecosystem
  - Non-blocking I/O

Cons:
  - Single-threaded
  - Unhandled rejections
  - Memory leaks from closures

Alternatives:
  - Go (goroutines)
  - Rust (async-std)
  - Python (asyncio)

State: +

